#. type: Title ##
#: docs/admin/05.get_started/20.install_on/_install_script.mdx:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "<FAIcon icon=\"fa-rocket\"/> Run the install script"
msgstr "<FAIcon icon=\"fa-rocket\"/> اسکریپت نصب را اجرا کنید"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/admin/05.get_started/20.install_on/_install_script.mdx:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Open a command line prompt on your server (either directly or [through SSH](/admin/command_line))\n"
"- Make sure you are root (or type `sudo -i` to become root)\n"
"- Run the following command:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: docs/admin/05.get_started/20.install_on/_install_script.mdx:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Always make sure there's an `s` at the end of `https`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: docs/admin/05.get_started/20.install_on/_install_script.mdx:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might need to first install `curl` and `ca-certificates` by running:\n"
"```bash\n"
"apt install curl ca-certificates\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (note)
#: docs/admin/05.get_started/20.install_on/_install_script.mdx:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "**For advanced users concerned with the `curl | bash` approach:** consider reading [\"Is curl|bash insecure?\"](https://sandstorm.io/news/2015-09-24-is-curl-bash-insecure-pgp-verified-install) on Sandstom's blog, and possibly [this discussion on Hacker News](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=12766350&noprocess).\n"
msgstr ""
